questions.question:
For a UI-only effect (a snackbar that may be skipped if nobody sees it), a teammate proposes:

```kotlin
private val _effects = Channel<String>(Channel.BUFFERED)
val effects = _effects.receiveAsFlow()

// screen
LaunchedEffect(Unit) {
    lifecycle.repeatOnLifecycle(Lifecycle.State.STARTED) {
        viewModel.effects.collect { snackbar.showSnackbar(it) }
    }
}
```

Statement: "Elements sent while the screen is in the background stay in the channel's buffer and are received when it collects again, and each element goes to one collector only."
